{
  // Skill-snippet compile ratchet baseline, measured on 2026-09-13 with:
  //   `node --import tsx builder/scripts/skill-snippet-gate.ts`
  //
  // Each number is the count of COMPILED skill snippets (see skill-snippet-gate.ts
  // for what "compiled" means: titled blocks, or untitled blocks that carry their
  // own imports) that currently FAIL to type-check, per shipping package. This is a
  // STATED, TRACKED allowance — the same shape as strictness-allowances.jsonc — not
  // an endorsement of the failures. A new failure in any package pushes that
  // package OVER its allowance and fails the gate. From this baseline, these
  // numbers may only go DOWN.
  //
  // Total across all packages at baseline: 314 failing compiled snippets
  // (526 compiled, 212 passing, 857 skipped as deliberate fragments, 0 cross-skill
  // type/path conflicts). Cross-skill type/path conflicts are held at a hard zero
  // by the gate and are NOT allowanced here.
  //
  // Every package that ships a skills/ tree MUST have an entry here: a measured
  // package with no recorded allowance fails the gate (an unmeasured allowance is
  // never silently treated as zero).
